Reason:
<text>

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
return (1000000000 / pixclock);
ps_to_hz(var->pixclock);
Reason:
ps_to_hz() divides by the pixclock parameter without checking for zero. It is called from hw_sm750_crtc_set_mode() with a pixclock value that may be zero because lynxfb_ops_check_var() did not validate the input. A zero pixclock causes a division by zero in ps_to_hz().

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!var->pixclock)
    return -EINVAL;
Reason:
Adding this check at the beginning of lynxfb_ops_check_var() rejects any framebuffer mode setting request with a pixclock of zero. This prevents the zero value from ever reaching ps_to_hz(), thereby eliminating the division by zero.

